  "observationBoundary": "Six cases replay the debug Map Test 0 prompt from one shared in-memory core state. A deterministic session-only copy of the verified ROM replaces the existing RunMapSetupInitFunction indirect call with the verified 16-byte FF-padding trampoline. The trampoline sets A6 to a RAM-owned word stream and JSRs one unmodified roof or step handler; the original disk ROM is re-hashed unchanged before launch. Lua writes only the handler input words, the source-named CURRENT_MAP, CURRENT_BATTLE, word_FFAF42, MAP_AREA_LAYER_TYPE, and VIEW_PLANE_UPDATE_TOGGLE_BITFIELD state, plus the selected nonasset layout marker words. It observes handler return, direct H1 call-site registers, the static table scan boundary, marker comparisons, and update-toggle bits. It does not establish complete layout, collision, pathfinding, presentation, audio, persistence, or normal-story reachability.",
